1
00:00:00,180 --> 00:00:02,900
Before a wildfire becomes a live emergency,

2
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:05,900
teams need somewhere to rehearse
the decisions that come first.

3
00:00:10,540 --> 00:00:12,100
Local knowledge lives in people.

4
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,500
Spatial evidence lives on maps.

5
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:17,900
And an AI assistant usually
reasons somewhere else.

6
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:20,950
Every handoff loses context.

7
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:29,000
PyroScan Incident Twin turns the browser
into one shared rehearsal table,

8
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:32,300
designed around La Palma's real geography
and constrained access.

9
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:45,200
WebMCP lets the page expose its real verbs
directly to ChatGPT.

10
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:51,100
Read, inspect, annotate, simulate,
compare, and stage.

11
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,100
No separate server.

12
00:00:53,100 --> 00:00:55,100
No brittle click script.

13
00:00:58,430 --> 00:01:00,100
I ask at the level of intent.

14
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:06,700
ChatGPT focuses El Paso and adds a blocked-road
exercise note for the LP-3 checkpoint.

15
00:01:07,270 --> 00:01:12,300
That local constraint becomes visible to me—
and available to every later tool call.

16
00:01:20,520 --> 00:01:25,900
Next, a sixty-minute northeast wind shift redraws
the deterministic attention area on the same map.

17
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:32,300
This is not a forecast; it is a bounded what-if
that a person and an agent can inspect together.

18
00:01:40,490 --> 00:01:47,950
PyroScan compares two reversible response options
against setup time, coverage, resource use,
and the new access constraint.

19
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:52,700
The ranking lives on screen—
not buried in a chat transcript.

20
00:01:58,510 --> 00:02:02,200
Before staging, ChatGPT reads
the exact board version.

21
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:05,730
If the evidence changed,
a stale plan is rejected.

22
00:02:05,730 --> 00:02:13,680
The new draft carries the LP-3 constraint into its access action,
proving that human knowledge changed the downstream artifact.

23
00:02:20,420 --> 00:02:21,500
The agent can explore.

24
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,100
It cannot approve.

25
00:02:24,280 --> 00:02:29,750
Final approval is deliberately absent from the WebMCP tools
and remains with the exercise director.

26
00:02:34,430 --> 00:02:39,300
Synthetic. Deterministic. Browser-only. Open source.

27
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:42,800
No live feed, dispatch, or hidden backend.

28
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:48,130
The ambition: rehearse trade-offs
before a crisis makes them irreversible.

29
00:02:49,110 --> 00:02:53,110
PyroScan. Wildfire readiness,
rehearsed together.
